<blockquote>
<p><strong>Koullette:</strong> Ok. Well, more food is a good thing I guess. It'll probably be easier to feed Thomas the berries than the rations.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yeah I wouldn't be suspicious of those either.</p>
<blockquote>
<table class="wiki-content-table">
<tr>
<td><strong>Supplemental Documentation</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Compromise of Site-19 Sublevels 36-38</td>
</tr>
</table>
</blockquote>
<p>I knew paying attention to these would pique my interest at some point.</p>
<p>Alright, and after reading this, it's an upvote. I don't know if I have too much to say about it either. I liked that as it went on, we were getting less and less information, feeling more in the dark. I loved the supplemental documentation gimmick &#8212; it made sense in-universe and really upped the mystery (ooo there's that 5K theme wooah whaaat). It gave a lot more credence to the fact that they were having trouble opening a door. Because either they weren't, or there is more to that door than is in this document. Also, you effectively had [DATA EXPUNGED], but it was access levels required, and never in the middle of paragraphs, and you still got the titles of the documents (it immediately caught my eye that the Ethics Committee was involved), and just, yeah, well done. Good article. +1</p>
<p>Seriously though what was with that berry exchange?</p>

